                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'll start by saying that I got this game for free somewhere along the line, and I would not recommend it at full price - I would probably wait for it to be at least 75% off.\n\nThe game is pretty short and will give you about 3-4 hours, but I did really enjoy the atmosphere. The story (mostly told through observational text boxes, notes that you find, and dialogue) is very engrossing. I usually find that I don't care about notes and details after a while, but I kept wanting to pay attention, which helps you figure out how to solve things anyway. There are also some really fun dark humor aspects that actually made me laugh.\n\nThe controls are really the only weak spot here, as they are clunky and grating at times, but you do adjust to them enough to mitigate the irritation.\n\nThe gameplay itself is akin to a point and click adventure, but also adds in a bit of stealth and combat (well, aiming/shooting a gun). It does enough to keep it interesting, and the story and setting really kept me in it. \n\nOverall, I enjoyed this game and I may eventually check out the sequel at some point.",
